    "recent_posts": [
      "Today we launch The Connector for Credit.\n\n9fin's proprietary credit intelligence is now available directly in Claude, ChatGPT, and other AI assistants.\n\nResearch a credit, screen opportunities, build an origination pitch, dig into covenants - just ask your AI, and get an answer verified back to source.\n\nThe credit depth your AI is missing, right where you already work.\n\nLearn more: https://lnkd.in/ebNT3HgU",
      "What does success look like when the goal is bigger than the role itself?\n\nSpeaking on Cloud9fin, J.P. Morgan's Daniel Rudnicki Schlumberger reflects on what it would mean for SRI to succeed over the next two or three years. He thinks it’s less about fixed plans and more about creating possibility: building the right ecosystem, finding the right people, and backing smart ideas. 💡\n\nFor Daniel, great investment banking means helping entrepreneurs, supporting companies and solving real problems — while contributing meaningfully to the nation and the safety of children.",
      "Who came out on top in Q2 2026's CLO legal league tables?🏆\n\nQ2 2026 saw SaaS-pocalypse tremors, oil price shocks and assets tightening faster than liabilities. Despite that, the CLO market proved that it can find a way to get business done.\n\nIn the US BSL arranger counsel rankings, Paul Hastings led with $85.85bn across 183 deals, followed by Orrick, Herrington & Sutcliffe LLP and Sidley Austin LLP.\n\nIn the US BSL manager counsel category, Milbank LLP led with $47.45bn across 112 deals, closely followed by Dechert LLP. Latham & Watkins overtook McDermott Will & Schulte in third.\n\n📊 Full Q2 20…",
      "A closer look at $5.7bn of loans at risk across 157 BDCs 👀\n\n9fin has screened nearly the entire BDC universe and based on Q1 2026 filings, and found that a handful of at-risk loans are held within multiple BDC portfolios.\n\nThe watchlist flags 468 individual loan positions across 157 BDC portfolios identified as potentially at risk.\n\nHead here for more: https://lnkd.in/ewb5AeRM",
      "THREE things you need to know about Debtflix, our H1 2026 European restructuring data review:\n\n⚖️ Restructuring and LME activity ticked up in H1 2026, with 20 deals compared to 16 in H1 2025. Nine were loan-only, five bond-only, and six a mix of bonds and loans.\n\n📊 Companies and creditors are increasingly proactive in managing stressed cap stacks. Six of the 11 restructurings triggered by a maturity were resolved with more than 12 months remaining until the company's earliest maturity, a noticeable change from H1 2024 and H1 2025.\n\n✍️ We saw nine pro rata LMEs, eight of which were stressed A&…",
      "From $6bn to $20bn in just two years — that’s the rapid growth of the private credit secondaries market between 2023 and 2025.\n\nWith a compound annual growth rate of over 70%, it’s critical that private credit professionals stay up to date with the secondaries market as it matures.\n\nThat’s where our crash course comes in, covering the basics, LP-led vs GP-led structures, pricing and valuation, documentation and legal mechanics, and where the market is heading.\n\nAccess the course now: https://lnkd.in/exHSwvhX",
      "How's this for some Friday excitement? The platform behind the world's leading credit teams is now advertised in 12 different locations across NYC 🗽\n\nPhotos below from 6th Ave, between 44th and 45th. If you pass by, make sure you take a pic and tag us!\n\nAnd to find out more about why the world’s leading credit teams 💙 9fin, head over here: https://lnkd.in/g9xzNQeC",
      "Raising a glass to the women shaping the CLO market 🍷\n\nWe’re gathering CLO experts for a ladies-only evening of wine, nibbles and networking at La Compagnie in Neal's Yard on Thursday 17 September.\n\nIf you’re looking to expand your network, this event pairs perfectly — blind tasting challenges alongside some of the sharpest minds in the CLO market. RSVP via the link below. \n\nhttps://lnkd.in/etqeQmaR"
    ]
  },
