      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/9fin_three-things-you-need-to-know-about-debtflix-activity-7486427497543282688-lAUy",
      "content": "THREE things you need to know about Debtflix, our H1 2026 European restructuring data review:\n\n⚖️ Restructuring and LME activity ticked up in H1 2026, with 20 deals compared to 16 in H1 2025. Nine were loan-only, five bond-only, and six a mix of bonds and loans.\n\n📊 Companies and creditors are increasingly proactive in managing stressed cap stacks. Six of the 11 restructurings triggered by a maturity were resolved with more than 12 months remaining until the company's earliest maturity, a noticeable change from H1 2024 and H1 2025.\n\n✍️ We saw nine pro rata LMEs, eight of which were stressed A&Es (four required a fresh shareholder equity injection: Isabel Marant, Maxeda DIY Group, Panariagroup Industrie Ceramiche S.p.A and Zenith). Non-pro rata activity dropped to three deals from four in H1 2025 — LIPTON Teas and Infusions, Lecta and Synthomer.\n\nThis data review delivers structural visibility into how the European restructuring landscape is evolving mid-year, with detailed breakdowns across sectors, jurisdictions, and transaction types.\n\nAccess the full piece here:https://lnkd.in/gdXxMR2q",
